  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Which of the following functions is continuous on the interval $[-1,2)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The correct answer is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945275/assets/105d87736460f2949a0cde4c7fe7cc105e72889312a529970d74080b14e3ffe8.png)\n\n \n\nIndeed, we have that $f(x)$ is continuous on the open interval $(-1,2).$ \n\nAdditionally, the function is right-continuous at $x=-1.$ Hence, it is continuous on the interval $[-1,2).$\n\nNotice that\n\n- $h(x)$ is not right-continuous at $x=-1.$\n\n- $p(x)$ and $g(x)$ are not continuous at some point that lies inside the interval $[-1,2).$\n\n- $q(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1$, and so is not continuous on $[-1,2).$",
